email.task:
You are an IT officer. Your company is moving to a new email system this month. Ellie, a sales manager, has asked how to set up her work email on her new phone. Write an email to Ellie explaining the steps, using the notes below. In your email you must use:
- the present continuous at least once for something that is happening now or around now (We're moving to…);
- at least one relative clause with which, that or who;
- at least one zero or first conditional sentence (If + present simple, present simple / will + verb).
Follow the standard layout for an email giving instructions: From / To / Date / Subject, a greeting, It should be quite easy to …, the steps with First / Then / Next / After that / Finally, a reminder (Don't forget to … when you've finished.), then Best wishes and your name, position and department.
Write 80–100 words (do not count the From, To, Date and Subject lines).
